Commands:
  help        - show this help
  echo ARG    - print ARG
  pwd, ls, cd - navigate RAM filesystem
  whoami      - print current user
  uname       - print kernel/platform identity
  history     - show recent shell commands
  cat FILE    - print a file
  cp/mv/stat/tree - inspect and move filesystem objects
  touch FILE  - create an empty file
  write F TXT - replace file contents
  mkdir DIR   - create a directory
  rm PATH     - remove empty dir or file
  edit FILE   - open numbered line editor; Up/Down move, Esc exits
  cls         - clear screen
  about       - kernel info
  fault       - test exception handler
  ticks       - show PIT ticks
  uptime      - show uptime seconds
  sleep N     - sleep N ticks
  mem         - show memory summary
  mmap        - print memory map
  heap        - show heap state
  alloc N     - bump-allocate N bytes
  paging      - show paging state
  mounts      - show filesystem stack mounts
  gui ARGS    - GUI foundation: status/start/stop/windows
  window ARGS - window objects: list/focus/move/info
  ps, kill P  - process table and stop process
  compute A   - scientific scheduler profile/status/bench
  math TOPIC  - linear algebra, number theory, groups, stats
  job ARGS    - generic OS job scheduler: list/run/priority
  service A   - service manager: list/start/stop/restart/status
  user/cap A  - users and capabilities
  event A     - reactive event rules
  net ARGS    - network stack: status/up/down/ip/udp/tcp
  security A  - security: status/audit/lock/unlock
  structure   - show current OS subsystem layout
  log ARGS    - logs: show/write/clear system|security|network
  regs        - show basic CPU flags
  test        - run safe command checks
  pkg ARGS    - package registry: list/info/install/remove/compat
  halt        - stop CPU
  reboot      - keyboard-controller reboot
Native language forms:
  inspect memory|heap|paging|processes|filesystem|gui|security|network
  file["PATH"].read() / exists() / write("TEXT") / append("TEXT")
  process["shell"].trace() / process["editor"].restart()
  service["network"].start() / window["shell"].focus()
  user["guest"].login() / event["net-audit"].emit()
  package["editor"].install() / info() / remove()
  spawn editor [FILE]
